.git
.gitignore
build/
dist/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
# Build output and caches that .gitignore already keeps out of the repository. They are not
# in the image either way - nothing copies them - but everything here is uploaded to the
# daemon as the build context before the first instruction runs, and these are the large
# ones: editors/vscode/out/ from working on the extension, htmlcov/ and .coverage from a
# coverage run, the packaged extension, the built documentation, and the two ASAP2
# specification pdfs under the design records.
editors/vscode/out/
*.vsix
htmlcov/
.coverage
coverage.xml
coverage.json
docs/_build/
docs/superpowers/*.pdf
# What npm leaves in the tree, which the image makes for itself: its pages stage installs the
# packages of gui/, generates the page types and compiles the pages, and the final stage takes
# the pages from it. `COPY src` and `COPY gui` take whatever the context holds, so the host's
# would be laid over the image's own - a stale build's pages installed beside the fresh ones,
# types generated from whatever package the host had, packages npm installed for another
# system. **/ because a bare node_modules/ matches at the root only, where there is none: the
# extension's and the browser interface's are further down.
**/node_modules/
src/ddd/gui/static/
gui/src/generated/
# What running the browser tests leaves, Playwright's traces and its report: nothing the image
# uses, and copied into its pages stage by `COPY gui` otherwise.
gui/test-results/
gui/playwright-report/
